1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,960
A Brave Maid.
勇敢的女仆。

2
00:00:02,960 --> 00:00:43,787
A wooden vase from the Ming Dynasty at the entrance of the reception hall amazed everyone. The artists designed it in a rare style and selected valuable jewels to decorate it. People thought highly of its fancy colour of honey and the beautiful paintings on it.
一只明代的木制花瓶，摆在接待大厅的入口处，让所有人都惊叹不已。艺术家以罕见的风格设计了它，并挑选贵重珠宝来装饰。人们高度赞赏它精美的蜜色外观，以及瓶身上美丽的画作。

3
00:00:43,787 --> 00:01:12,080
The vase used to belong to a former castle. But when the country was at war, the enemy troops exploded the castle. Debates on how the vase survived went on and on.
这个花瓶曾属于一座旧城堡。但在国家陷入战争时，敌军炸毁了城堡。关于花瓶如何幸存，人们争论不休。

4
00:01:12,080 --> 00:02:02,007
In order to remove people’s doubt, a team of no less than 20 people carried out an informal investigation. The evidence they found showed that a maid took the vase apart and asked a sailor to sink it in a local well. She never gave away the secret even under the cruel trial of the enemies who were in search of treasures.
为了消除大家的疑问，一支不少于20人的队伍展开了非正式调查。他们发现的证据表明，一名女仆把花瓶拆开了，请一名水手将它沉入当地的一口井中。她始终没有泄露秘密，即便遭受敌人的残酷审讯，那些敌人正在搜寻财宝。

5
00:02:02,007 --> 00:02:10,000
It is worth giving this brave maid a fortune in return.
这位勇敢的女仆值得得到一大笔钱作为回报。
